# Cursor adapter

Save as `.cursorrules` in the project root (or merge into your existing rules).

```
When the user asks to build a website or app — "saya ingin membuat website",
"saya ingin membuat aplikasi", "I want to build a website",
"I want to build an app", "build me an app", "create a web app" — do not start
coding. Load the web-forge skill and run its pipeline.

Order:
1. node <web-forge>/scripts/forge.mjs doctor
2. node <web-forge>/scripts/forge.mjs new "<name>" --stack <laravel|next|html|api>
3. Fill docs/BRIEF.md, docs/SPEC.md, docs/PLAN.md.
4. node <web-forge>/scripts/forge.mjs gate  (require brief/spec/plan PASS)
5. Build in thin slices, running `gate --url <url>` after each UI change.
6. Before claiming completion: node <web-forge>/scripts/forge.mjs gate --release --strict

Non-negotiable:
- SKIP is not PASS; say "not measured".
- No phase approval without an existing proof file in .forge/ledger.json.
- Never report an audit result you did not run.
- Never write source files through a shell pipe (mojibake); use file editing.
- Report numbers: status codes, counts, widths, contrast, byte sizes.
```
